{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>A woman of valor</b> — from \"your wealth\" (חילך), meaning money. That is, the woman who acquires money is a crown to her husband, for because of her they honor him, just as a king is honored by the crown on his head." "<b>In his bones</b> — no remedy avails. So too a shameful woman brings shame upon her husband, and she diminishes the money."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:18.406993888Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}